    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find \\(a - b\\), we start by using the given points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\) to set up a system of equations. The general form of the line equation is \\(y = ax + b\\).\n\nFor the point \\((4,5)\\), we have:\n\\[\n5 = 4a + b\n\\]\nFor the point \\((8,17)\\), we have:\n\\[\n17 = 8a + b\n\\]\n\nWe now have the following system of linear equations:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4a + b = 5 \\\\\n8a + b = 17\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nTo eliminate \\(b\\), we subtract the first equation from the second:\n\\[\n(8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5\n\\]\n\\[\n8a + b - 4a - b = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n4a = 12\n\\]\n\\[\na = 3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(a = 3\\), we substitute it back into the first equation to find \\(b\\):\n\\[\n4(3) + b = 5\n\\]\n\\[\n12 + b = 5\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 5 - 12\n\\]\n\\[\nb = -7\n\\]\n\nThus, we have \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\). The value of \\(a - b\\) is:\n\\[\na - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
