      "text": "1. The slope \\(a\\) of the line can be calculated by using the formula for the slope between two points. The formula for the slope between points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}\n   \\]\n   Applying this to the given points \\((4,5)\\) and \\((8,17)\\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{17 - 5}{8 - 4} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\n   \\]\n\n2. To find the \\(b\\) value, use the point-slope formula \\(y = ax + b\\) and substitute the values of \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(a\\) from one of the points. Using \\((4,5)\\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 3(4) + b\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\(b\\):\n   \\[\n   5 = 12 + b \\implies b = 5 - 12 \\implies b = -7\n   \\]\n\n3. Finally, to find \\(a - b\\):\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 - (-7)\n   \\]\n   Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   a - b = 3 + 7 = 10\n   \\]\n\nConclusion: The value of \\(a - b\\) is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
